# Copy to /etc/vps-backup-pull.env on the backup host and set for that host.
# The unit reads it with EnvironmentFile=-, so the leading - makes it optional:
# a host running the layout below needs no file at all and the script's defaults stand.
#
# This file configures the WRITING side, the pull itself. The reading side is
# Blog's own secrets/<server>.<environment>.env, which names the same two
# destinations so the log review can find what the pull produced. The pairs must
# agree, and OPERATIONS.md "Working With the VPS" states which pairs those are.
#
# systemd parses this file itself rather than passing it to a shell. There is no
# expansion, no command substitution, and no quoting to strip, so write a bare
# value and never wrap it in quotes -- the quotes become part of the path.

# Where to pull from. The administrative login, not the confined deploy account.
VPS_HOST=root@vps.example.com

# On the VPS: the encrypted archives, written by its own backup timer.
REMOTE_ARCHIVE_DIR=/var/backups/pangolin

# On the VPS: the rotated edge access logs. Today's live file is deliberately not
# among them, because rotation is what makes a file eligible to be copied.
REMOTE_TRAEFIK_LOG_DIR=/var/log/traefik/archive

# On the VPS: one-off Caddy container dumps kept from before rotation existed.
REMOTE_BLOG_LOG_DIR=/var/log/blog/legacy

# On the backup host: the archives and the plaintext hostconfig tree beside them.
# Blog's secrets file names this same directory as BACKUP_ARCHIVE_ROOT.
DEST=/path/to/backup/vps

# On the backup host: both log sets. Separate from DEST, and mode 700, because these
# are plaintext and long-lived where the archives are encrypted and pruned, and
# because query strings are logged in full so the tree is as sensitive as the log.
# Blog's secrets file names this same directory as LOG_ARCHIVE_ROOT.
LOG_DEST=/path/to/backup/vps-logs

# Key auth only; the VPS has password auth disabled. BatchMode makes an unusable key
# fail immediately instead of hanging a timed run on a password prompt nobody sees.
SSH_OPTS=-o ConnectTimeout=15 -o BatchMode=yes
